<small>To the chief Musician on Neginoth, Maschil, <i>A Psalm</i> of David, when the Ziphims came and said to Saul, Doth not David hide himself with us?</small><br /><sup><b>1</b></sup> Save me, O God, by thy name, and judge me by thy strength.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Hear my prayer, O God; give ear to the words of my mouth.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> For strangers are risen up against me, and oppressors seek after my soul: they have not set God before them. Selah.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> Behold, God <i>is</i> mine helper: the Lord <i>is</i> with them that uphold my soul.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> He shall reward evil unto mine enemies: cut them off in thy truth.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> I will freely sacrifice unto thee: I will praise thy name, O LORD; for <i>it is</i> good.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> For he hath delivered me out of all trouble: and mine eye hath seen <i>his desire</i> upon mine enemies. <br />
